There is no arrow-key navigation for command buttons! The how-to says "Keyboard: Arrow keys / WASD to pick, Enter or Space to confirm". This is a false claim / missing feature. Need to implement keyboard navigation for command menus. Since buttons are native `<button>`, Tab focus works but arrows don't. We should add global keydown handler for command panel: arrow keys/WASD move focus among enabled `.cmd`, Enter/Space click focused (native button already handles Enter/Space). Also numeric shortcuts? Let's implement.

Simplest: add a `keydown` listener on document that, when currentScreen === 'match' and no overlay visible (meter/cutin/pause), handles Arrow keys/WASD to focus next/prev enabled button in #commands. Also `Escape` pause? maybe.

Because buttons may re-render each menu, focus resets. On menu render, auto-focus first button? That could cause focus outline. For keyboard users, yes. But auto-focus might interfere with touch? No. We can focus first when menu is rendered only if last input was keyboard. Simpler: arrow keys always move from currently focused or first.

Implement:

```
document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
  if (currentScreen !== 'match' || paused) return;
  if (!$('meter-layer').classList.contains('hidden')) return;
  if (!$('cutin-layer').classList.contains('hidden')) return;
  if (!$('pause-layer').classList.contains('hidden')) return;
  const cmds = [...document.querySelectorAll('#commands .cmd:not([disabled])')];
  if (!cmds.length) return;
  const key = e.key;
  const isNext = key==='ArrowDown'||key==='ArrowRight'||key==='s'||key==='S'||key==='d'||key==='D';
  const isPrev = key==='ArrowUp'||key==='ArrowLeft'||key==='w'||key==='W'||key==='a'||key==='A';
  if (!isNext && !isPrev) return;
  e.preventDefault();
  const active = document.activeElement;
  let idx = cmds.indexOf(active);
  if (idx < 0) idx = isNext ? -1 : 0;
  const next = isNext ? (idx + 1) % cmds.length : (idx - 1 + cmds.length) % cmds.length;
  cmds[next].focus();
});
```

